### What is a partition reassignment?

A partition reassignment moves partition replicas from one set of brokers to another. Kafka does this to rebalance load, add or drain brokers, or recover from failures. It is an online operation, but it causes transient consumer lag and latency spikes.

```bash
# Generate and execute a reassignment plan
kafka-reassign-partitions.sh --bootstrap-server kafka-1:9092 \
  --reassignment-json-file plan.json --execute \
  --throttle 50000000   # 50 MB/s cap on replication
```

### Cause 1: Disk and network saturation from data copying

The destination broker must fetch the entire partition log from the leader, which can be gigabytes. This competes with normal produce and consume traffic for the same disks and network.

```java
package com.bank.kafka;

public class DataCopySaturation {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        long partitionSizeGB = 50;
        long networkMBps = 100; // available bandwidth
        long copyTimeSec = partitionSizeGB * 1024 / networkMBps;

        System.out.println("Partition size: " + partitionSizeGB + " GB");
        System.out.println("Available bandwidth: " + networkMBps + " MB/s");
        System.out.println("Copy time (unthrottled): " + copyTimeSec + " seconds");
        System.out.println("During copy: normal produce/consume competes for same I/O");
        System.out.println("Result: consumer lag spikes, producer latency increases");
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
Partition size: 50 GB
Available bandwidth: 100 MB/s
Copy time (unthrottled): 512 seconds
During copy: normal produce/consume competes for same I/O
Result: consumer lag spikes, producer latency increases
```

### Cause 2: Throttling trades rate for duration

A replication throttle caps the bytes per second for moving data. This reduces contention but extends the duration.

```java
package com.bank.kafka;

public class ThrottlingTradeoff {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        long partitionSizeGB = 50;
        long unthrottledMBps = 100;
        long throttledMBps = 50;

        long unthrottledSec = partitionSizeGB * 1024 / unthrottledMBps;
        long throttledSec = partitionSizeGB * 1024 / throttledMBps;

        System.out.println("Unthrottled: " + unthrottledSec + "s (high contention, short)");
        System.out.println("Throttled (50 MB/s): " + throttledSec + "s (less contention, longer)");
        System.out.println("Trade-off: intensity vs duration");
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
Unthrottled: 512s (high contention, short)
Throttled (50 MB/s): 1024s (less contention, longer)
Trade-off: intensity vs duration
```

### Cause 3: Leader movement forces reconnection

When leaders move, consumers get NOT_LEADER_FOR_PARTITION errors, refresh metadata, and reconnect. During this window, requests fail and retry.

```java
package com.bank.kafka;

public class LeaderMovementImpact {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Leader movement during reassignment:");
        System.out.println("  1. Consumer sends fetch to old leader (broker-1)");
        System.out.println("  2. Broker-1: NOT_LEADER_FOR_PARTITION");
        System.out.println("  3. Consumer refreshes metadata");
        System.out.println("  4. Discovers new leader is broker-3");
        System.out.println("  5. Reconnects to broker-3");
        System.out.println("  6. Brief latency spike for affected partitions");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("At scale: many partitions moving -> burst of metadata refreshes");
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
Leader movement during reassignment:
  1. Consumer sends fetch to old leader (broker-1)
  2. Broker-1: NOT_LEADER_FOR_PARTITION
  3. Consumer refreshes metadata
  4. Discovers new leader is broker-3
  5. Reconnects to broker-3
  6. Brief latency spike for affected partitions

At scale: many partitions moving -> burst of metadata refreshes
```

### Cause 4: Cold page cache on the new broker

Kafka relies on the OS page cache for fast reads. A new broker has none of the partition's data in cache, so consumer fetches hit disk.

```java
package com.bank.kafka;

public class ColdCacheImpact {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Page cache impact after leader movement:");
        System.out.println("  Old broker: partition data in page cache -> memory reads");
        System.out.println("  New broker: no cached data -> disk reads");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("  Memory read latency: ~100 microseconds");
        System.out.println("  Disk read latency:   ~10 milliseconds (100x slower)");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("  Cache warms up as consumers read data");
        System.out.println("  Latency returns to normal after warm-up period");
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
Page cache impact after leader movement:
  Old broker: partition data in page cache -> memory reads
  New broker: no cached data -> disk reads

  Memory read latency: ~100 microseconds
  Disk read latency:   ~10 milliseconds (100x slower)

  Cache warms up as consumers read data
  Latency returns to normal after warm-up period
```

### Cause 5: Coordination overhead

Every replica movement changes the ISR, triggers metadata propagation, and possibly leader elections. At scale these add up.

### How do you mitigate these causes?

Three mitigations map onto the five causes:

| Mitigation | Addresses |
|---|---|
| Monitor replication throughput | Saturation (cause 1) |
| Avoid peak traffic hours | All causes -- spare capacity absorbs impact |
| Throttle appropriately | Saturation vs duration trade-off (causes 1, 2) |
| Move in small batches | Leader movement and cold cache (causes 3, 4, 5) |
| Delay leader promotion | Cold cache (cause 4) |

```bash
# Execute with throttle and verify
kafka-reassign-partitions.sh --bootstrap-server kafka-1:9092 \
  --reassignment-json-file plan.json --execute \
  --throttle 50000000

# Monitor progress
kafka-reassign-partitions.sh --bootstrap-server kafka-1:9092 \
  --reassignment-json-file plan.json --verify

# IMPORTANT: --verify also removes the throttle config when complete
# A forgotten throttle silently caps replication forever!
```

### What are common mistakes?

```java
package com.bank.kafka;

public class ReassignmentMistakes {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // WRONG: reassign all partitions at once during peak
        System.out.println("WRONG: move 200 partitions at peak traffic");
        System.out.println("  Result: massive lag, many NOT_LEADER errors, cold caches");

        // CORRECT: small batches during off-peak with throttle
        System.out.println("CORRECT: move 10 partitions at a time, off-peak, throttled");
        System.out.println("  Result: minimal impact, controlled warm-up");

        // WRONG: forget to run --verify after completion
        System.out.println("WRONG: skip --verify after reassignment");
        System.out.println("  Result: throttle stays forever, caps all future replication");
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
WRONG: move 200 partitions at peak traffic
  Result: massive lag, many NOT_LEADER errors, cold caches
CORRECT: move 10 partitions at a time, off-peak, throttled
  Result: minimal impact, controlled warm-up
WRONG: skip --verify after reassignment
  Result: throttle stays forever, caps all future replication
```

### What should a senior engineer know?

Delay promoting a freshly moved replica to leader until it has caught up and the cache has warmed. Raise the throttle near the end when the cluster is calmer. Always run `--verify` to clean up throttle configuration. Plan reassignment like any capacity-sensitive operation.
